[Music]  how's it going everyone mark madden rip  here and we're back at the playstation  competition center for more tekken 7  videos  today we're going to talk about walls  and how it'll change your strategy in a  fight  most stages in tekken are small  battlefield surrounded on all sides by  walls  as you bike you may get pushed towards  one of these boundaries and find itself  trapped between your opponent and the  wall  like being cornered in most 2d fighting  games this is a very bad spot to be in  and you'll want to avoid getting in this  position as best you can  normally when you're being pressured in  tekken you can back dash away from your  opponent to create space  when you're near a wall that option no  longer exists not only that but many  attacks in tekken 7 that are normally  pretty innocent  will cause what's called a wall splat  when you hit someone towards the wall  these moves now suddenly become high  damage combo starters making a lot of  attacks very scary  how do you defend with your back to the  wall first it's very important to wait  for your turn then slowly try to use  your side step to get away from the wall  next try not to crouch at the back of  the wall as most attacks the wall splat  you will be mid-attacked  this will lead to another combo and  leave you in the same situation patience  and timing will be key  another important tactic is to use  throws while near the wall  knowing your throw range and how they  manipulate the positioning between you  and your opponent is key  certain throws will allow you to swap  places between you and your opponent  regardless if they were successful or  escaped keep this knowledge in mind when  you're looking for an opportunity to  escape the danger zone near a walled  area of the state  on offense if you are hitting your  opponent in the air towards a wall  sometimes the wall splatter will occur  at an unexpected time or angle and cause  the rest of your combo to not work  properly  when you're first starting out don't  worry about this too much but as you  play more you'll start to recognize  where you are in the stage and realize  how to adjust your combo  to account for the wall distance  of course some stages in tekken 7 do not  have any walls at all  these are usually called infinite stages  and benefit certain playstyles that  don't rely on using the walls  and on some stages certain walls can  actually break if you hit your opponent  into them the right way  your opponent might even fall down to a  new part of the stage giving you new  combo opportunities  it's important to keep in mind at all  times where the walls are on offense you  want to push your opponents towards the  wall  and on defense you want to use your  movement to get yourself away from the  wall  that's it for this episode this tutorial  is made in partnership with the  playstation competition center team  you can check out  compete.playstation.com to watch learn  and compete  subscribe to the bne esports channel for  more tutorials and tekken 7 content

